## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant secrets strategy, runtime access flow, rotation, and CI safety beyond data isolation.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets Manager per-tenant isolation
- Workload Identity for runtime retrieval
- CMEK-backed encryption and rotation
- CI gate validating cross-tenant access and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();
async function accessSecret(tenantId, suffix) {
  const name = `projects/${PROJECT_ID}/secrets/tenant-${tenantId}-${suffix}/versions/latest`;
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({name});
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rotation impact on live traffic?
- How would you revoke access for a suspended tenant?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical tenancy controls in a NoSQL store; checks how to enforce data isolation with security rules, IAM, and network boundaries; assesses ability to design automated containment.

## Key Concepts
- Firestore security rules and tenant-scoped paths
- Per-tenant service accounts with least privilege
- Private Service Connect and VPC Service Controls
- CI/CD gate with synthetic tenants and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Firestore rules snippet (illustrative)
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /tenants/{tenantId}/{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.token.tenants.contains(tenantId);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for potential rule bypasses in CI?
- What are the trade-offs of using per-tenant collections vs single collection with tenant_id field?
